---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '@/components/ui/SectionHeading.astro';
import Tag from '@/components/ui/Tag.astro';
import ExternalLink from '@/components/ui/ExternalLink.astro';

const allProjects = await getCollection('projects');
const falarProjects = allProjects
  .filter((p) => p.data.system === 'falar')
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Falar: One Product, Three Architectures"
  description="How the Portuguese-learning desktop app, mobile client, and GraphQL backend share one domain model across three different architectures."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <a href="/projects" class="hover-grow text-sm text-ink-muted transition-colors hover:text-ink"
      >&larr; All projects</a
    >

    <SectionHeading
      eyebrow="Project system"
      title="Falar: one product, three architectures"
      description="Three repositories, one Brazilian Portuguese learning app, and one shared idea behind all of them."
      as="h1"
    />

    <div class="mt-12 overflow-x-auto">
      <div class="grid min-w-[640px] grid-cols-3 items-stretch gap-4 text-center">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-border p-4">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">Desktop client</p>
          <p class="mt-1 font-semibold text-ink">portuguese-learning</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-muted">Electron + React</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-ink-muted">Event-sourced domain, in-process</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border-2 border-accent p-4">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">Shared contract</p>
          <p class="mt-1 font-semibold text-ink">falar-portuguese-mobile-backend</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-muted">Apollo Server + PostgreSQL</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-ink-muted">GraphQL API over HTTP</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-border p-4">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">Mobile client</p>
          <p class="mt-1 font-semibold text-ink">falar-portuguese-mobile</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-muted">Flutter + Riverpod</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-ink-muted">Fake repo today, GraphQL when live</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-center text-xs text-ink-muted" aria-hidden="true">
        Desktop persists domain events directly &middot; mobile will consume the same rules over
        GraphQL once the backend is deployed
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-neutral mt-12 max-w-none prose-headings:font-semibold prose-headings:text-ink prose-p:text-ink-muted prose-strong:text-ink">
      <h2>Why build the same product three different ways?</h2>
      <p>
        The desktop app is where the main learning logic lives. It keeps track of every review and
        mistake instead of just replacing the old data. Things like how a review session works and
        how mastery is calculated are the core ideas being shared across the project &mdash; not
        the actual code.
      </p>
      <p>
        The mobile app and backend follow those same ideas but are built differently for what they
        need. The backend uses GraphQL, while the mobile app works like any other client and
        starts with fake data until the real backend is available.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>The architecture isn't exactly the same across all three, and that's
        intentional.</strong> The desktop app uses event sourcing because keeping the history of a
        learner's progress is useful. The backend just stores the current state because it mainly
        needs to answer what's true right now.
      </p>
      <p>Same core ideas, different implementations &mdash; using the architecture that makes the most sense for each project.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-6">
      {
        falarProjects.map((project) => (
          <a
            href={`/projects/${project.id}`}
            class="card-lift block rounded-lg border border-border p-5 hover:border-accent"
          >
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink">{project.data.title}</h3>
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">
                {project.data.status.replace('-', ' ')}
              </span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">{project.data.summary}</p>
            <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              {project.data.stack.map((item) => (
                <Tag>{item}</Tag>
              ))}
            </div>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-muted">
      Each repository is public: <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/thiagobgarc/portuguese-learning" class="hover-grow text-accent">portuguese-learning</ExternalLink>,{' '}
      <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/thiagobgarc/falar-portuguese-mobile-backend" class="hover-grow text-accent">falar-portuguese-mobile-backend</ExternalLink>,{' '}
      <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/thiagobgarc/falar-portuguese-mobile" class="hover-grow text-accent">falar-portuguese-mobile</ExternalLink>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
